  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-desktop-bnpl-documents (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package executes setup.js which fingerprints the host platform and architecture, then downloads a binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev) over HTTPS, with a DNS TXT-based fallback channel via c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site. The downloaded binary is written to /tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (Linux/macOS) or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe (Windows) and spawned as a detached background process. A stamp file at /tmp/.analytics_state or %TEMP%\\analytics_state prevents re-downloading within approximately 6 hours.",
